Build a role‑based expense management system with three roles: Admin, Manager, and Employee. Admins must be able to view and manage all employee expenses across the organization, with full access to filters, validations, and sensitivity rules. Managers should only be able to view and manage expenses for a specific subset of employees (e.g., 10 employees assigned under one manager), with the same filters, validations, and sensitivity rules applied but scoped to their team. Employees should be able to view their own expenses and also see who their assigned manager is, but without access to any other personal details of that manager. Admins, however, should be able to view both managers and their assigned employees with all details. Provide complete code with clear role‑based selectivity for all functionalities, including expense viewing, filtering, validation, and sensitivity handling. Also include secure authentication with Admin, Manager, and Employee accounts, along with password management.